# Copy to `.env` for local development (do not commit `.env`).
# First-party apps load `.env`, then evaluate `askdb.config.*` / `.config/askdb.*` (`@askdb/config`).
# AskDB reads its settings from that config file, not from the environment: each variable below
# matters only because the repo's askdb.config.ts reads it with env("…"). The one AskDB variable
# read straight from the shell is ASKDB_DEBUG.
# For an `askdb.config.ts` starter with example `.env` keys in comments, run: `pnpm exec askdb init`

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI provider  (BYO LLM keys)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The repo's askdb.config.ts uses `ai.provider: "openai"`. It reads OPENAI_API_KEY into the
# openai connection (`ai.providerConfig.openai.apiKey`) and OPENAI_MODEL into `ai.language.model`.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Also works for OpenRouter, Together, Groq, vLLM, LM Studio, llama.cpp server, Foundry's
# `/openai/v1` inference route: anything that speaks the OpenAI REST protocol. The OpenAI SDK
# reads OPENAI_BASE_URL itself.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=                       # e.g. https://api.openai.com/v1 (default)

# To use another provider, set `ai.provider` in askdb.config.ts and give it a connection under
# `ai.providerConfig`, reading each value with env("…"). These are the providers' usual names.
#
# Azure OpenAI / Microsoft Foundry (`ai.provider: "azure"`): the connection takes `apiKey` and
# `resourceName` (the subdomain, e.g. "my-foundry" for https://my-foundry.openai.azure.com) or
# `baseUrl`, plus `apiVersion`; `ai.language.model` is the *deployment* name.
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# AZURE_RESOURCE_NAME=
# AZURE_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://.../openai/deployments   # instead of the resource name
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-10-21
# AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=
#
# Google Gemini (`ai.provider: "google"`):
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_AI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash       # or gemini-2.5-pro, etc.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database  (BYO — only required for live introspection)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The repo's askdb.config.ts reads DATABASE_URL for `introspection.providerConfig.postgres.databaseUrl`
# and for Studio's Execute (`studio.execute.databaseUrl`).
# For another engine, set `introspection.provider` to it and move the
# `databaseUrl: env("DATABASE_URL")` line under that engine's providerConfig (SQLite takes
# `file` instead). The values below connect to the multi-engine fixture (`pnpm fixture:up`).
#
# Postgres
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://fixture_reader:fixture_reader@127.0.0.1:15432/askdb_fixture
# MySQL (provider "mysql"; list more databases with `introspection.schemas`)
# DATABASE_URL=mysql://fixture_reader:fixture_reader@127.0.0.1:13306/org
# MariaDB (provider "mysql")
# DATABASE_URL=mysql://fixture_reader:fixture_reader@127.0.0.1:13307/org
# SQL Server (provider "sqlserver"; an mssql:// URL works too)
# DATABASE_URL=Server=127.0.0.1,11433;Database=askdb_fixture;User Id=fixture_reader;Password=Fixture.Reader.2026;Encrypt=false;TrustServerCertificate=true
# SQLite (provider "sqlite", `providerConfig.sqlite.file`; no URL): ./fixtures/multi-engine/.data/multi-engine.sqlite

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RAG  (optional)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The pgvector store's connection (`rag.storeConfig.pgvector.databaseUrl`), when `rag.store` is
# "pgvector". Its index strategy is `rag.storeConfig.pgvector.indexStrategy` in askdb.config.ts
# (ivfflat | hnsw | none, default hnsw).
# ASKDB_PGVECTOR_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5434/askdb_rag

# The embedding model. The repo's askdb.config.ts sets `rag.embedder: "ai"` and reads these into
# `ai.embedding`, which embeds through the openai connection (OPENAI_API_KEY above).
# Set `rag.embedder: "mock"` there for the local lexical embedder, which needs no key.
# ASKDB_RAG_EMBEDDER_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small   # ai.embedding.model (default in askdb.config.ts)
# ASKDB_RAG_EMBEDDER_DIMENSIONS=1536                # ai.embedding.dimensions; optional: requests a size, else the model's own width
# To embed with another provider (an Azure deployment, Gemini, …), set `ai.embedding.provider`
# (and `connection` when it has several) in askdb.config.ts and give it a connection in `ai.providerConfig`.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs, modes, tests
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The correlation id on every JSON log line (`logging.correlationId`). The log level is
# `logging.level` in askdb.config.ts, or `--log-level` on the CLI.
# ASKDB_CORRELATION_ID=

# The operating mode is `modes.askdbMode` in askdb.config.ts (schema_only | bounded_results;
# see docs/contracts/modes-v1.md). Omitting sensitive table/column *names* from NL→SQL DDL is
# `modes.omitSensitiveFromPrompt: true` there (or `askdb ask --omit-sensitive-from-prompt`).

# Fixed SQL instead of a model call, for tests and local runs (`dev.mockSql`).
# ASKDB_MOCK_SQL=SELECT 1

# Print stack traces on errors. Read from the shell directly, not through askdb.config.ts.
# ASKDB_DEBUG=1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HTTP API and Studio  (optional)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The HTTP API's default schema is `host.schemaPath` in askdb.config.ts (or `askdb-http --schema-path`).
# The config reads HOST and PORT for `httpApi.listen`, and ASKDB_STUDIO_HOST and ASKDB_STUDIO_PORT
# for `studio.listen`.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=3000
# ASKDB_STUDIO_HOST=127.0.0.1
# ASKDB_STUDIO_PORT=5556
